          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures, beginning at age 17. Current seizure frequency is approximately four seizures per week. The epilepsy is drug-resistant.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Valproate\n- Levetiracetam\n- Lacosamide\n- Oxcarbazepine\n\nSeizure Burden:\nGeneralized tonic-clonic seizures occur approximately four times weekly despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-resistant generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures. The etiology is genetic, associated with a causative STXBP1 variant, c.902A>G. Brain MRI demonstrates nonspecific white matter changes.\n\nPlan:\nMaintain the current antiseizure medications: valproate, levetiracetam, lacosamide, and oxcarbazepine.",
